---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageFrame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import WorkSection from '../components/WorkSection.astro';
import ActionRow from '../components/ActionRow.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import Dot from '../components/Dot.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import CaseLead from '../components/CaseLead.astro';
import MetaLine from '../components/MetaLine.astro';
import Carousel from '../components/Carousel.astro';
const head = `<link rel="icon" href="data:," />`;
const afterFooter = ``;
---
<Base title={"Hotpress - Gorka Molero Case Study"} description={"Hotpress, an app for writing together in real time with print-ready book and e-book export, and how I tested its collaboration on Liveblocks end to end."} page="hotpress">
  <Fragment slot="head" set:html={head} />
  <PageFrame class="sheet">
    <Masthead />

      <CaseLead class="lead">
        <MetaLine class="meta eyebrow">Case · collaborative writing and publishing</MetaLine>
        <h2 class="case-title">Hotpress</h2>
        <p class="intro">Hotpress is an app for writing together in real time, with print-ready book and e-book export. It's live at <a href="https://hotpress.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hotpress.app</a>, and its source is public.</p>
        <MetaLine class="meta chips">Own project <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Next.js, Lexical, Liveblocks, Yjs, Postgres, Playwright</MetaLine>
      </CaseLead>

      <main>
      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>Writing together</h2>
        <p>The editor is Lexical, kept in sync through Liveblocks and Yjs. Writers share a document with a link, and guests can join without an account. Each writer has their own colour, and you see their pointer move, their caret with their name on it and their selection tinted in that colour. Edits merge as they happen. Each comment is a pin beside its phrase, with the writer's initials, and it opens the thread right there, or as a bottom sheet on a phone.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="./assets/hotpress/collaboration-v22-poster.jpg" src="https://pub-066596d7e4fe4de2b74eac13bb03fe55.r2.dev/hotpress-collaboration-v22.mp4" aria-label="Two writers in one Hotpress document: a guest joins through the share link, both write at once, they comment and reply, and the guest's offline writing merges when they reconnect."></video></div>
          <figcaption>Two people in one manuscript. A guest joins through the share link, both write at once, they comment and reply in place, and while the guest is offline both keep writing, then everything merges when they reconnect. Recorded locally on a production build of the app.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>How I tested it</h2>
        <p>To check the collaboration properly, I wrote a Playwright suite that runs against Liveblocks itself, with nothing mocked. Three people share a room, two signed in and one guest. They type in the same sentence at once, comment, reply and resolve, and the guest drops offline for nine seconds while the others keep writing. Then someone joins late, and the saved document and the exported PDF have to contain everyone's text.</p>
        <p>Fast typing lost characters. The cause was in Liveblocks' own Lexical comments plugin, which set a fresh array of active threads on every editor update. React stopped that with a "Maximum update depth exceeded" error, and the error cut off Lexical's other listeners before the last edits reached the shared Yjs document. The same bug left a writer out of date after a long offline gap. I patched the plugin in Hotpress so it keeps the old array when the threads haven't changed, a one-line change. The bug is still in Liveblocks' latest release, 3.24.3, so I <a href="https://github.com/liveblocks/liveblocks/issues/3753" target="_blank" rel="noopener">reported it</a> and opened a <a href="https://github.com/liveblocks/liveblocks/pull/3754" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pull request with the fix</a>.</p>
        <p>Comments also failed now and then with a 403. My auth route gave out two kinds of Liveblocks token, and the client sometimes sent a comment with the kind that carries no room permissions. I changed it to issue one kind for everything, with the same access as before.</p>
        <p>With both fixes, the suite passed all 17 checks three runs in a row on a production build. In those runs an edit reached the other writer in a median of 0.2 seconds, and 0.45 seconds at the 95th percentile. After I added the coloured carets, selections and comment pins, the full suite of 20 tests passed on a production build, and a check against the live hotpress.app passed five runs out of five.</p>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work">
        <h2>From manuscript to book</h2>
        <p>Hotpress also lays out the book. You pick one of 22 templates, set up chapters, scene breaks, front and back matter, headers and footers, page layout and typography, and export a PDF for the printer, with a PDF/X-4 output intent, CMYK colour, bleed and trim marks, or an EPUB. It uses GitHub for version control.</p>
        <Carousel class="carousel" aria-label="Chapter openings from five of the Hotpress templates">
          <div class="carousel-track">
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/hotpress/template-thornbury.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="A chapter opening in the Thornbury template: the title page beside the first page of text, which opens with a four-line drop cap." /></div><figcaption>Thornbury, a serif template in Libre Baskerville</figcaption></Figure>
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/hotpress/template-pemberton.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="A chapter opening in the Pemberton template: a Playfair Display title and EB Garamond text." /></div><figcaption>Pemberton, a serif template in EB Garamond</figcaption></Figure>
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/hotpress/template-rosewood.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="A chapter opening in the Rosewood template: a script chapter title and Lora text." /></div><figcaption>Rosewood, a script template</figcaption></Figure>
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/hotpress/template-ironclad.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="A chapter opening in the Ironclad template: a condensed capital title and serif text." /></div><figcaption>Ironclad, a genre template</figcaption></Figure>
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot"><img src="./assets/hotpress/template-hyperlegible.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="A chapter opening in the Hyperlegible template, set large in Atkinson Hyperlegible." /></div><figcaption>Hyperlegible, an accessible template in Atkinson Hyperlegible</figcaption></Figure>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-nav"><button type="button" class="carousel-prev" aria-label="Previous template">&larr;</button><span class="carousel-count">1 / 5</span><button type="button" class="carousel-next" aria-label="Next template">&rarr;</button></div>
        </Carousel>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="https://hotpress.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open hotpress.app</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button" href="https://github.com/gorkamolero/inkwell" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The source on GitHub</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>
      </main>
  </PageFrame>
  <Fragment slot="after-footer" set:html={afterFooter} />
</Base>
